WEBVTT

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.130
Last time on Star Trek:
The Next Generation:

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.969
Mr. Worf,
dispatch a subspace message

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.168
to Admiral Hanson.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.576
We have engaged the Borg.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.778
Data, fluctuate phaser
resonance frequencies.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.580
Random settings,
keep them changing.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.109
Don't give them time to adapt.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.848
We're coming
with every available starship

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:27.985
to assist, Captain

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:32.294
but the closest help
is six days away.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.527
All you know how to do
is play it safe.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.195
If you can't make
the big decisions, Commander

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.001
I suggest you make room
for someone who can.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.383
If we can generate
a concentrated burst of power

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:53.716
at that same
frequency distribution...

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.015
How do we do that?

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.522
The main deflector dish.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.766
Shelby to Enterprise.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.894
We've found
the Captain's uniform

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.460
and his communicator.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.280
Jean-Luc.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.875
We were unable
to retrieve him, sir.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.818
The Captain has been
altered by the Borg.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.821
Will, he's alive.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.379
If we could get him
back to the ship

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.685
I might be able to restore...

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.453
This is our only chance
to destroy them.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.688
If they get back into warp,
our weapon is useless.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:39.494
I am Locutus of Borg.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:45.402
From this time forward,
you will service us.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:55.606
Mr. Worf... fire.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.651
And now, the conclusion.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:58.673
And now, the conclusion.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.146
Deflector power
approaching maximum limits.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.658
Energy discharge in six seconds.

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:13.665
Firing, sir.

00:02:20.205 --> 00:02:22.969
The Borg ship is undamaged.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:24.976
Impossible.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.741
Warning. Warp reactor core
primary coolant failure.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.215
I can't maintain it much longer,
Commander.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:36.051
Warning. Exceeding
reaction chamber thermal limit.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.818
Cease fire.

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:42.952
Shutting down warp engines.

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:49.093
They couldn't have
adapted that quickly.

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:53.332
The knowledge and experience
of the human, Picard

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:56.239
is part of us now.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:03:01.474
It has prepared us for all
possible courses of action.

00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:04.778
Your resistance is hopeless...

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.978
Number One.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.953
Space, the final frontier.

00:03:43.988 --> 00:03:47.822
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:03:47.858 --> 00:03:49.826
Its continuing mission--

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.796
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:53.831 --> 00:03:58.268
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:58.302 --> 00:04:02.796
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:05:01.164 --> 00:05:05.100
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 44001.4.

00:05:05.135 --> 00:05:08.332
The Borg ship has resumed
its course toward Earth.

00:05:08.371 --> 00:05:12.102
We are unable to pursue pending
repairs to the Enterprise.

00:05:12.142 --> 00:05:14.133
As we anticipated,
the blast burned out

00:05:14.177 --> 00:05:15.906
our main navigational deflector.

00:05:15.946 --> 00:05:18.380
We also have damage
to our shields

00:05:18.415 --> 00:05:20.042
and our reactor core.

00:05:20.083 --> 00:05:22.950
We should be back up
in eight to 12 hours, Admiral.

00:05:23.053 --> 00:05:25.521
Well, we'll miss you
at the party.

00:05:25.555 --> 00:05:26.852
The Enterprise will be there.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.915
Maybe a little late,
but we'll be there, sir.

00:05:28.959 --> 00:05:32.326
Your engagements
have given us valuable time.

00:05:32.362 --> 00:05:36.298
We've mobilized a fleet
of 40 starships at Wolf 359.

00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:38.563
And that's just for starters.

00:05:38.602 --> 00:05:40.229
The Klingons are sending
warships.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.498
Hell, we've even thought

00:05:41.538 --> 00:05:44.371
of opening communications
with the Romulans.

00:05:44.407 --> 00:05:47.240
You realize, Admiral, that with
the assistance of Captain Picard

00:05:47.277 --> 00:05:49.108
the Borg will be ready
for your defenses.

00:05:49.145 --> 00:05:53.514
Lieutenant, a few years ago,
I watched a freshman cadet

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.610
pass four upperclassmen
on the last hill

00:05:56.653 --> 00:05:58.416
of a 40-kilometer run
at Danula ll.

00:05:58.455 --> 00:06:00.946
The damnedest thing I ever saw.

00:06:00.991 --> 00:06:05.553
The only freshman to ever win
the Academy marathon.

00:06:05.595 --> 00:06:08.223
I made it my business
to get to know that young fellow

00:06:08.265 --> 00:06:09.892
and I got to know
him very, very well.

00:06:09.933 --> 00:06:11.195
And I'll tell you something--

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:15.193
I never met anyone
with more drive, determination

00:06:15.238 --> 00:06:18.105
or more courage
than Jean-Luc Picard

00:06:18.141 --> 00:06:22.874
and there is no way in hell
that he would assist the Borg.

00:06:22.913 --> 00:06:24.778
I want that clear.

00:06:24.814 --> 00:06:27.282
Of course, Admiral.

00:06:27.317 --> 00:06:32.380
He is... a casualty of war.

00:06:32.422 --> 00:06:37.553
Then we have abandoned
all hope of recovering him.

00:06:37.594 --> 00:06:39.721
In less than 24 hours

00:06:39.763 --> 00:06:43.255
this armada's going to hit
that Borg vessel

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.768
with everything we can muster.

00:06:45.802 --> 00:06:48.236
Either they survive or we do.

00:06:48.271 --> 00:06:51.104
And as for Picard...

00:06:51.141 --> 00:06:54.804
a great man has been lost.

00:06:54.844 --> 00:06:58.177
Your Captain.
My friend.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.318
Commander Riker,
I hereby promote you

00:07:02.352 --> 00:07:05.412
to the field commission
of Captain.

00:07:05.455 --> 00:07:07.889
The Enterprise is your ship now.

00:07:07.924 --> 00:07:09.551
Congratulations.

00:07:09.592 --> 00:07:12.652
I wish the circumstances
were different.

00:07:12.696 --> 00:07:14.630
Likewise.

00:07:14.664 --> 00:07:16.859
Good luck, Admiral.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:19.425
Mm. To us all.

00:08:14.257 --> 00:08:16.191
And Mr. Crusher suggests
we might design a chip

00:08:16.226 --> 00:08:18.194
that would automatically
re-tune the phasers

00:08:18.228 --> 00:08:20.059
to a random setting
after each discharge.

00:08:20.096 --> 00:08:21.120
Engineering.

00:08:21.164 --> 00:08:23.792
That would be a great advantage.

00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:25.323
We should also see
if there's some way

00:08:25.368 --> 00:08:27.063
that we can neutralize
their force fields.

00:08:27.103 --> 00:08:29.503
We've got to let them know that
we can adapt, too, Mr. Worf.

00:08:29.539 --> 00:08:31.268
We're no longer
just fighting the Borg.

00:08:31.307 --> 00:08:32.831
We're fighting
the life experience

00:08:32.876 --> 00:08:34.400
they've stolen
from Captain Picard.

00:08:34.444 --> 00:08:36.207
Now, how the hell
do we defeat an enemy

00:08:36.246 --> 00:08:38.237
that knows us better
than we know ourselves?

00:08:38.281 --> 00:08:41.079
The Borg have neither
honor nor courage.

00:08:41.117 --> 00:08:43.312
That is our greatest advantage.

00:08:43.353 --> 00:08:44.650
I hope it's enough.

00:08:48.358 --> 00:08:51.327
Accelerator coils
are responding normally.

00:08:51.361 --> 00:08:53.158
Excellent.

00:08:53.196 --> 00:08:55.255
Forward shields at 58%.

00:08:55.298 --> 00:08:58.392
Aft shields...
Sensors must be down.

00:08:58.434 --> 00:09:00.459
Checking. Sensors are fine.

00:09:00.503 --> 00:09:03.404
No, aft shields
have completely failed.

00:09:03.439 --> 00:09:04.406
Damn it!

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.431
Auxiliary generators
are out again.

00:09:06.476 --> 00:09:08.205
Just the man I need.

00:09:08.244 --> 00:09:10.337
We're having some problems
with the aft shields.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.007
The generator's
going on and off-line.

00:09:12.048 --> 00:09:13.606
I could really use
your help, Worf.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.515
How soon do we
get underway, Geordi?

00:09:15.552 --> 00:09:16.576
Still a couple of hours.

00:09:16.619 --> 00:09:18.052
Commander Shelby
can fill you in.

00:09:21.658 --> 00:09:23.922
The main navigational deflector
is functional again.

00:09:24.027 --> 00:09:25.927
Sherbourne and Barclay
are running through

00:09:25.962 --> 00:09:27.327
the final testing
sequence now.

00:09:27.363 --> 00:09:28.352
The warp reactor core?

00:09:28.398 --> 00:09:30.366
Reconstruction
is proceeding normally.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.492
It's slow work.

00:09:31.534 --> 00:09:33.866
If we can nail down
this shield generator problem

00:09:33.903 --> 00:09:35.063
I agree with La Forge.

00:09:35.104 --> 00:09:38.301
We should be back at operating
capacity in two to three hours.

00:09:38.341 --> 00:09:40.809
Good.

00:09:43.146 --> 00:09:44.408
Anything else, sir?

00:09:44.447 --> 00:09:47.678
Yes. You did a good job
on the Borg ship.

00:09:47.717 --> 00:09:49.810
I didn't get Picard.

00:09:49.852 --> 00:09:51.581
You stopped them.

00:09:51.621 --> 00:09:53.816
You gave us our shot.

00:09:53.856 --> 00:09:55.824
Sir, l...

00:09:55.858 --> 00:09:57.621
Commander, we don't have
to like each other

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.627
to work well together.

00:09:58.661 --> 00:09:59.628
As a matter of fact

00:09:59.662 --> 00:10:01.493
I'd like you to continue
to keep me on my toes.

00:10:01.531 --> 00:10:03.692
Some might define that
as the role

00:10:03.733 --> 00:10:04.961
of a First Officer.

00:10:05.034 --> 00:10:08.595
Damn, you are ambitious,
aren't you, Shelby?

00:10:08.638 --> 00:10:11.072
Captain Riker, based
on our past relationship

00:10:11.107 --> 00:10:12.904
there's no reason
for me to expect

00:10:12.942 --> 00:10:14.500
to become your First Officer

00:10:14.544 --> 00:10:16.341
except that you need me.

00:10:16.379 --> 00:10:17.607
I know how to get things done

00:10:17.647 --> 00:10:19.239
and I have the expertise
in the Borg.

00:10:19.282 --> 00:10:21.375
And you have a lot to learn,
Commander.

00:10:23.086 --> 00:10:24.417
Yes, sir.

00:10:24.454 --> 00:10:27.082
Almost as much as I had
to learn when I came onboard

00:10:27.123 --> 00:10:28.784
as Captain Picard's
First Officer.

00:10:28.825 --> 00:10:30.087
A fact he reminded me of

00:10:30.126 --> 00:10:32.686
when I commented on what a pain
in the neck you are.

00:10:32.729 --> 00:10:34.890
Yes, sir.

00:10:34.931 --> 00:10:37.593
Data to Riker.
Message from Starfleet, Captain.

00:10:37.634 --> 00:10:39.625
Go ahead, Data.

00:10:39.669 --> 00:10:41.830
Starfleet reports
it has engaged the Borg

00:10:41.871 --> 00:10:43.304
at Wolf 359, sir.

00:10:49.912 --> 00:10:53.541
Admiral Hanson
on subspace, Captain.

00:10:53.583 --> 00:10:56.780
On screen.

00:10:56.819 --> 00:10:58.810
Admiral?

00:10:58.855 --> 00:11:00.948
The fight does not
go well, Enterprise.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:04.118
We're attempting
to withdraw and regroup.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.060
Rendezvous with fleet...

00:11:20.676 --> 00:11:24.168
Captain's Log, Stardate 44002.3.

00:11:24.213 --> 00:11:26.374
Repairs are complete
and the Enterprise

00:11:26.415 --> 00:11:29.316
is warping to rendezvous
with Starfleet at Wolf 359.

00:11:29.352 --> 00:11:32.480
Communications from the site
of battle have been cut off

00:11:32.521 --> 00:11:34.455
possibly due
to Borg interference.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.890
Lieutenant Worf,
everyone in this room

00:11:36.926 --> 00:11:39.986
shares my respect
for your service to this ship

00:11:40.062 --> 00:11:42.587
but, right now, I need
your experience at tactical.

00:11:42.631 --> 00:11:46.590
Commander Data, I realize
your very nature omits ambition.

00:11:46.635 --> 00:11:48.262
Nevertheless, I want you to know

00:11:48.304 --> 00:11:51.705
I seriously considered you
as First Officer.

00:11:51.741 --> 00:11:53.709
Thank you, sir.

00:11:53.743 --> 00:11:56.371
But this is not
the time for change.

00:11:56.412 --> 00:11:58.539
I need all of you where you are

00:11:58.581 --> 00:12:01.379
where Captain Picard
always relied on you.

00:12:01.417 --> 00:12:04.386
I have been... reluctantly...
forced to conclude

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:07.321
that Commander Shelby,
our expert on the Borg

00:12:07.356 --> 00:12:09.415
is an ideal choice at this time

00:12:09.458 --> 00:12:12.393
for First Officer.

00:12:14.263 --> 00:12:17.960
Based on our latest
communication, we can assume

00:12:18.033 --> 00:12:21.298
that the Borg survived
the fleet's attack.

00:12:21.337 --> 00:12:23.328
Your thoughts
on our next encounter.

00:12:23.372 --> 00:12:26.398
What about the heavy graviton
beam we were talking about?

00:12:26.442 --> 00:12:27.807
I've gone over it four times.

00:12:27.843 --> 00:12:30.573
The local field distortion
just wouldn't be strong enough

00:12:30.613 --> 00:12:31.637
to incapacitate them.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.739
Dr. Crusher and l
have been working on

00:12:33.783 --> 00:12:35.080
an interesting premise.

00:12:35.117 --> 00:12:37.415
With our recent experience
in nanotechnology

00:12:37.453 --> 00:12:38.977
we might be able to introduce

00:12:39.054 --> 00:12:41.454
a destructive breed of nanites
into the Borg.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.752
Nanites?

00:12:42.792 --> 00:12:43.781
Robots

00:12:43.826 --> 00:12:46.420
small enough
to enter living cells.

00:12:46.462 --> 00:12:48.327
How long would it take
to execute that?

00:12:48.364 --> 00:12:50.093
That's the problem--
two to three weeks.

00:12:50.132 --> 00:12:51.963
In two or three weeks,
nanites may be

00:12:52.001 --> 00:12:53.730
all that's left
of the Federation.

00:12:53.769 --> 00:12:55.600
We have the new phaser adapters.

00:12:55.638 --> 00:12:57.128
Maybe in concert

00:12:57.173 --> 00:12:59.767
with the photon torpedoes,
we can slow them down.

00:13:01.644 --> 00:13:03.202
I'm sure Captain Picard

00:13:03.245 --> 00:13:06.146
would have something
meaningful and inspirational

00:13:06.182 --> 00:13:07.206
to say right now.

00:13:07.249 --> 00:13:09.308
To tell you the truth,
I wish he was here

00:13:09.351 --> 00:13:11.046
'cause I'd like to hear it, too.

00:13:11.086 --> 00:13:13.577
I know how difficult
this transition

00:13:13.622 --> 00:13:15.749
has been for all of you.

00:13:15.791 --> 00:13:17.554
I can take over for him

00:13:17.593 --> 00:13:19.720
but I could never replace
Captain Picard

00:13:19.762 --> 00:13:21.286
nor would I ever try.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:23.855
Whatever the outcome

00:13:23.899 --> 00:13:28.233
I'm sure our efforts
in the coming battle

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:31.728
will justify his faith
in all of us.

00:13:31.774 --> 00:13:33.935
Dismissed.

00:13:46.121 --> 00:13:47.986
What would you do?

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.452
Come.

00:13:56.732 --> 00:13:59.098
May I speak to you, Captain?

00:13:59.134 --> 00:14:00.761
Actually, Guinan, l...

00:14:00.803 --> 00:14:02.703
You know, Picard and l
used to talk

00:14:02.738 --> 00:14:05.172
every now and then,
when one of us needed to.

00:14:09.044 --> 00:14:13.276
I guess I'm just used
to having the Captain's ear.

00:14:13.315 --> 00:14:15.875
What's on your mind?

00:14:15.918 --> 00:14:19.877
I've heard a lot of people
talking down in Ten-Forward.

00:14:19.922 --> 00:14:23.323
They expect to be dead
in the next day or so.

00:14:23.359 --> 00:14:25.224
They trust you.

00:14:25.261 --> 00:14:26.956
They like you.

00:14:27.029 --> 00:14:30.294
But they don't believe
anyone can save them.

00:14:30.332 --> 00:14:32.926
I'm not sure anyone can.

00:14:32.968 --> 00:14:37.064
When a man is convinced
he's going to die tomorrow

00:14:37.106 --> 00:14:40.701
he'll probably find a way
to make it happen.

00:14:40.743 --> 00:14:44.235
The only one who can
turn this around is you.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.646
I'll do the best I can.

00:14:46.682 --> 00:14:51.085
You're going to have to do
something you don't want to do.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.850
You have to let go of Picard.

00:14:53.889 --> 00:14:56.357
Maybe you haven't heard.

00:14:56.392 --> 00:14:59.657
I tried to kill him yesterday.

00:14:59.695 --> 00:15:03.256
You tried to kill whatever
that is on the Borg ship--

00:15:03.299 --> 00:15:04.493
not Picard.

00:15:06.902 --> 00:15:10.531
Picard is still here with us.

00:15:10.573 --> 00:15:12.040
In this room.

00:15:12.074 --> 00:15:14.941
If he had died,
it would be easier.

00:15:15.044 --> 00:15:16.511
But he didn't.

00:15:16.545 --> 00:15:20.208
They took him from us
a piece at a time.

00:15:20.249 --> 00:15:24.083
Did he ever tell you
why we're so close?

00:15:24.119 --> 00:15:26.178
No.

00:15:26.221 --> 00:15:28.212
Oh.

00:15:28.257 --> 00:15:32.887
Then let me just say
that our relationship

00:15:32.928 --> 00:15:36.887
is beyond friendship,
beyond family.

00:15:36.932 --> 00:15:39.400
And I will let him go.

00:15:39.435 --> 00:15:42.404
And you must do the same.

00:15:42.438 --> 00:15:45.703
There can only be one Captain.

00:15:45.741 --> 00:15:46.969
It's not that simple.

00:15:47.009 --> 00:15:48.101
This was his crew.

00:15:48.143 --> 00:15:49.974
He wrote the book on this ship.

00:15:50.079 --> 00:15:52.843
If the Borg know
everything he knows

00:15:52.881 --> 00:15:55.679
it's time to throw
that book away.

00:15:55.718 --> 00:15:57.982
You must let him go, Riker.

00:15:58.053 --> 00:16:00.783
It's the only way to beat him.

00:16:00.823 --> 00:16:04.520
The only way to save him.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:08.462
And that is now your chair...

00:16:08.497 --> 00:16:10.226
Captain.

00:16:42.431 --> 00:16:46.231
We are now approaching
the Wolf system, Captain.

00:16:46.268 --> 00:16:48.600
On my way.

00:16:53.542 --> 00:16:54.839
Slow to impulse.

00:16:54.877 --> 00:16:58.176
Take us to the battle
coordinates, Mr. Crusher.

00:16:58.213 --> 00:16:59.680
Yellow Alert.

00:16:59.715 --> 00:17:03.344
Sensors are picking up
several vessels, Captain.

00:17:03.385 --> 00:17:04.852
The fleet?

00:17:04.887 --> 00:17:06.855
No active subspace fields.

00:17:06.889 --> 00:17:08.857
Negligible power readings.

00:17:08.891 --> 00:17:10.188
Life signs?

00:17:10.225 --> 00:17:11.522
Negative, sir.

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:12.857
Visual contact.

00:17:12.895 --> 00:17:15.022
On screen.

00:17:33.482 --> 00:17:36.883
The Tolstoy.

00:17:36.919 --> 00:17:38.944
The Kyushu.

00:17:38.987 --> 00:17:41.956
The Melbourne.

00:18:09.684 --> 00:18:13.313
Sir, sensors are picking up
unusually strong eddy currents

00:18:13.355 --> 00:18:16.017
bearing 200 mark 21 1.

00:18:16.057 --> 00:18:17.183
Data, analysis?

00:18:17.225 --> 00:18:19.591
It could indicate the course
of the Borg ship, sir.

00:18:19.628 --> 00:18:22.392
Ensign Crusher, set in a course
that follows those currents.

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:24.159
Commander Shelby,
prepare to initiate

00:18:24.199 --> 00:18:26.064
your plan to separate
the saucer section

00:18:26.101 --> 00:18:27.159
when we find the Borg.

00:18:27.202 --> 00:18:28.328
Sir, I must remind you

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.668
that Captain Picard
was briefed on that plan.

00:18:30.705 --> 00:18:32.366
The Borg will be
prepared for it.

00:18:32.407 --> 00:18:33.931
I'm aware of that, Commander.

00:18:33.975 --> 00:18:35.943
In fact, I'm counting on it.

00:18:35.977 --> 00:18:38.878
Crusher, Cartaino, Gleason,
report to the Battle Bridge.

00:18:38.913 --> 00:18:41.279
Mr. Data, Mr. Worf

00:18:41.316 --> 00:18:43.978
I have a special mission
for you.

00:19:04.539 --> 00:19:05.904
Locutus of Borg

00:19:05.974 --> 00:19:09.205
this is Captain William T. Riker
of the USS Enterprise.

00:19:09.244 --> 00:19:13.078
You may speak.

00:19:13.114 --> 00:19:15.514
We wish to end the hostilities.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:19.452
Then you must
unconditionally surrender.

00:19:19.487 --> 00:19:23.253
We are prepared to meet
to discuss your terms.

00:19:23.291 --> 00:19:27.557
It is unlikely you are prepared
to discuss terms.

00:19:27.595 --> 00:19:33.192
It is more likely that this is
an attempt at deception.

00:19:33.234 --> 00:19:34.531
Come now, Locutus.

00:19:34.569 --> 00:19:37.538
If Picard's knowledge
and experience

00:19:37.572 --> 00:19:39.199
is part of you

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:43.108
then you know
that I've never lied to him.

00:19:43.144 --> 00:19:46.477
You should also
implicitly trust me.

00:19:46.514 --> 00:19:48.141
Is that not so?

00:19:48.183 --> 00:19:51.050
Picard implicitly trusted you.

00:19:51.086 --> 00:19:52.713
Then trust me now.

00:19:52.754 --> 00:19:54.915
Meet to discuss your terms.

00:19:54.956 --> 00:19:57.254
Discussion is irrelevant.

00:19:57.292 --> 00:19:58.953
There are no terms.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:05.329
You will disarm all your weapons
and escort us to Sector 001

00:20:05.366 --> 00:20:09.063
where we will begin assimilating
your culture and...

00:20:09.104 --> 00:20:11.197
Mr. Gleason, can you
pinpoint the source

00:20:11.239 --> 00:20:12.604
of the Borg transmission?

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:15.575
I can put you
within 30 meters of it, sir.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:16.907
O'Brien, report.

00:20:16.945 --> 00:20:20.244
The Borg have adapted
their electromagnetic field

00:20:20.281 --> 00:20:23.216
to prevent main
transporter function, sir.

00:20:23.251 --> 00:20:24.343
As expected.

00:20:24.385 --> 00:20:27.081
Mr. Data, Mr. Worf,
proceed as we discussed.

00:20:27.122 --> 00:20:29.590
Aye, Captain.

00:20:29.624 --> 00:20:30.921
Channel open, sir.

00:20:30.959 --> 00:20:32.893
We would like time
to prepare our people

00:20:32.927 --> 00:20:34.224
for assimilation.

00:20:34.262 --> 00:20:36.253
Preparation is irrelevant.

00:20:36.297 --> 00:20:40.996
Your people will be assimilated
as easily as Picard has been.

00:20:41.069 --> 00:20:43.128
Your attempt at a delay

00:20:43.171 --> 00:20:46.265
will not be successful,
Number One.

00:20:46.307 --> 00:20:48.207
We will proceed to Earth

00:20:48.243 --> 00:20:53.772
and if you attempt to intervene,
we will destroy you.

00:20:53.815 --> 00:20:56.147
Then take your best shot,
Locutus

00:20:56.184 --> 00:20:58.550
'cause we are
about to intervene.

00:21:00.054 --> 00:21:01.021
Channel closed.

00:21:01.055 --> 00:21:02.488
Reset subspace communications.

00:21:02.524 --> 00:21:03.821
Scrambler code, Riker One.

00:21:03.858 --> 00:21:06.850
Scrambler code Riker One,
acknowledged.

00:21:06.895 --> 00:21:07.862
Shelby, report.

00:21:07.896 --> 00:21:09.363
Ready for separation.

00:21:09.397 --> 00:21:11.194
Make it so.

00:21:11.232 --> 00:21:13.291
Auto-sep sequence initiated.

00:21:20.341 --> 00:21:22.070
Docking latches clear.

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.702
Separation complete.

00:21:23.745 --> 00:21:27.579
Saucer velocity, 100 meters
per second and increasing, sir.

00:21:27.615 --> 00:21:28.843
Open fire. All weapons.

00:21:28.883 --> 00:21:30.510
Fire.

00:21:41.729 --> 00:21:43.993
Borg tractor beam
attempting to lock on, sir.

00:21:44.065 --> 00:21:47.000
Evasive maneuvers,
pattern Riker Alpha.

00:21:47.101 --> 00:21:49.569
Riker Alpha, confirmed.

00:21:53.408 --> 00:21:56.707
They're ignoring
the saucer section completely.

00:21:56.744 --> 00:21:59.508
Just as you should, Captain.

00:21:59.547 --> 00:22:02.812
Ensign, evasive pattern
Riker Beta.

00:22:02.851 --> 00:22:05.319
Riker Beta, confirmed.

00:22:05.353 --> 00:22:07.253
Proceed to second phase,
Commander Shelby.

00:22:07.288 --> 00:22:08.346
Acknowledged.

00:22:08.389 --> 00:22:10.254
Fire antimatter spread.

00:22:21.703 --> 00:22:24.194
Shuttle launch sequence
confirmed.

00:22:24.239 --> 00:22:27.697
Departing Enterprise
in exactly three seconds.

00:22:51.266 --> 00:22:54.235
The Borg tractor beam has moved
toward the antimatter spread.

00:22:54.269 --> 00:22:56.499
They might be picking up
the engine ionization

00:22:56.537 --> 00:22:57.526
from the shuttle.

00:22:57.572 --> 00:22:59.199
Data, cut your engines.

00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:00.867
Take her in unpowered.

00:23:04.379 --> 00:23:07.542
Shuttle has penetrated
the Borg electromagnetic field.

00:23:07.582 --> 00:23:08.810
Understood.

00:23:12.453 --> 00:23:16.184
The shuttle escape transporter
should provide enough power

00:23:16.224 --> 00:23:17.885
to beam us onto the Borg ship
from here, sir.

00:23:17.926 --> 00:23:19.257
Proceed.

00:24:22.557 --> 00:24:23.888
Data!

00:24:40.975 --> 00:24:42.602
Mission accomplished.

00:24:42.643 --> 00:24:44.110
We have him.

00:24:44.145 --> 00:24:47.046
Firing shuttle thrusters.

00:24:51.085 --> 00:24:53.280
They're clear
of the Borg field, sir.

00:24:53.321 --> 00:24:55.414
Beam them out of there,
Mr. O'Brien.

00:24:55.456 --> 00:24:58.152
Locked in.

00:25:07.235 --> 00:25:09.396
Transport successful, sir.

00:25:28.822 --> 00:25:31.518
Captain, we've sustained damage
to the impulse drive.

00:25:31.558 --> 00:25:33.753
The saucer section is disabled.

00:25:33.794 --> 00:25:36.388
Reading subspace field
fluctuations from the Borg ship.

00:25:36.430 --> 00:25:38.921
Looks like they're getting
ready to increase power.

00:25:38.966 --> 00:25:39.955
Stand by, Mr. La Forge.

00:25:40.067 --> 00:25:40.965
Aye, sir.

00:25:41.068 --> 00:25:43.832
The saucer section's
a sitting duck.

00:25:45.239 --> 00:25:47.867
Prepare to draw their fire.

00:25:47.908 --> 00:25:50.376
Captain, the Borg ship
is moving away.

00:25:52.746 --> 00:25:55.874
It's resuming its course
towards Earth, sir.

00:25:55.916 --> 00:25:58.544
Rendezvous
with the saucer section.

00:25:58.585 --> 00:26:00.610
Lay in a course of pursuit.

00:26:03.657 --> 00:26:05.215
There is extensive infiltration

00:26:05.259 --> 00:26:08.126
of the microcircuit fibers
into the surrounding tissue.

00:26:08.161 --> 00:26:09.594
His DNA is being rewritten.

00:26:09.630 --> 00:26:10.722
Can you revive him?

00:26:10.764 --> 00:26:12.595
I'd like more time to study

00:26:12.633 --> 00:26:14.624
the structural changes
in the motor pathways.

00:26:14.668 --> 00:26:16.397
We don't have more time, Doctor.

00:26:16.436 --> 00:26:18.301
Once he was wired into the Borg

00:26:18.338 --> 00:26:20.329
they knew everything
that he knew.

00:26:20.374 --> 00:26:22.205
I just hope it goes both ways.

00:26:22.242 --> 00:26:23.937
If we're lucky, he had access

00:26:24.044 --> 00:26:26.512
to everything we need
to know about them.

00:26:26.547 --> 00:26:28.913
Especially their
vulnerabilities.

00:26:36.557 --> 00:26:39.583
Jean-Luc, it's Beverly.

00:26:39.626 --> 00:26:41.719
Can you hear me?

00:26:47.067 --> 00:26:51.595
Beverly... Crusher... Doctor.

00:26:51.638 --> 00:26:53.833
Yes.

00:26:53.874 --> 00:26:57.366
Don't try to move.

00:26:57.411 --> 00:27:00.574
I am on board the Enterprise.

00:27:00.614 --> 00:27:02.741
That's right.

00:27:07.588 --> 00:27:10.182
A futile maneuver.

00:27:10.223 --> 00:27:13.283
Incorrect strategy, Number One

00:27:13.327 --> 00:27:19.027
to risk your crew and ship
to retrieve only one man.

00:27:19.066 --> 00:27:22.035
Picard would never
have approved.

00:27:22.069 --> 00:27:26.403
You underestimate
us, if you believe

00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:30.069
this abduction is any concern.

00:27:33.447 --> 00:27:37.577
There is no need
for apprehension.

00:27:37.618 --> 00:27:39.916
I intend no harm.

00:27:39.953 --> 00:27:41.580
No harm.

00:27:41.622 --> 00:27:44.489
I will continue

00:27:44.524 --> 00:27:48.290
aboard this ship,
to speak for the Borg

00:27:48.328 --> 00:27:51.786
while they continue,
without further diversion

00:27:51.832 --> 00:27:54.323
to Sector 001

00:27:54.368 --> 00:27:58.236
where they will force
your unconditional surrender.

00:28:05.278 --> 00:28:07.712
Using multimodal
reflection sorting

00:28:07.748 --> 00:28:09.340
I have been able to detect

00:28:09.383 --> 00:28:11.578
a complex series
of subspace signals

00:28:11.618 --> 00:28:13.711
between Locutus
and the Borg ship.

00:28:13.754 --> 00:28:16.052
That's how
they're controlling him?

00:28:16.089 --> 00:28:18.489
It is not just a matter
of control, Doctor.

00:28:18.525 --> 00:28:21.426
The signals are interactive
across a subspace domain

00:28:21.461 --> 00:28:23.588
similar to that
of a transporter beam.

00:28:23.630 --> 00:28:25.894
I would hypothesize
that these frequencies

00:28:25.932 --> 00:28:28.901
form the basis of the Borg's
collective consciousness.

00:28:28.935 --> 00:28:30.402
Can't we block them?

00:28:30.437 --> 00:28:33.099
Possibly, but as you may recall,
on several occasions

00:28:33.140 --> 00:28:35.574
we have witnessed
the Borg removing key circuits

00:28:35.609 --> 00:28:36.701
from injured comrades.

00:28:36.743 --> 00:28:39.507
No doubt separating them
from the group consciousness.

00:28:39.546 --> 00:28:41.912
The injured Borg
immediately self-destructed.

00:28:41.948 --> 00:28:43.882
That is correct, sir.

00:28:43.917 --> 00:28:46.511
Cutting the link to Locutus
might be fatal to the Captain.

00:28:46.553 --> 00:28:49.716
We have to find a way
to reach him.

00:28:49.756 --> 00:28:52.384
We must know what he knows.

00:28:52.426 --> 00:28:54.291
Without
these interactive signals

00:28:54.327 --> 00:28:56.795
it would only be a matter
of microsurgery--

00:28:56.830 --> 00:28:57.797
I could do it.

00:28:57.831 --> 00:28:59.765
But as long
as these Borg implants

00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:01.563
are functioning, there's no way

00:29:01.601 --> 00:29:04.593
I can separate the man
from the machine.

00:29:04.638 --> 00:29:07.198
Then perhaps there is a way

00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:10.573
I can access the machine,
Doctor.

00:29:21.254 --> 00:29:24.712
Worf. Klingon species.
A warrior race.

00:29:24.758 --> 00:29:27.056
You, too, will be assimilated.

00:29:27.094 --> 00:29:30.393
The Klingon Empire
will never yield.

00:29:30.430 --> 00:29:32.057
Why do you resist?

00:29:32.099 --> 00:29:35.398
We only wish to raise
quality of life

00:29:35.435 --> 00:29:37.232
for all species.

00:29:37.270 --> 00:29:40.103
I like my species the way it is.

00:29:40.140 --> 00:29:42.233
A narrow vision.

00:29:42.275 --> 00:29:46.075
You will become one
with the Borg.

00:29:46.113 --> 00:29:49.708
You will all become one
with the Borg.

00:29:50.617 --> 00:29:52.710
The android...

00:29:52.753 --> 00:29:56.245
Data...
primitive artificial organism.

00:29:56.289 --> 00:29:59.816
You will be obsolete
in the new order.

00:30:01.795 --> 00:30:03.660
Take him to your lab, Data.

00:30:05.365 --> 00:30:06.832
Shelby to Riker.

00:30:06.867 --> 00:30:08.334
Go ahead.

00:30:08.368 --> 00:30:11.360
Captain, the Borg
have entered Sector 001.

00:30:26.119 --> 00:30:28.110
The Borg have dropped
out of warp, sir.

00:30:28.155 --> 00:30:30.350
Jupiter Outpost 92
reported visual contact

00:30:30.390 --> 00:30:31.721
at 1200 hours, 13 minutes.

00:30:31.758 --> 00:30:33.248
Planetary defenses?

00:30:33.293 --> 00:30:34.851
Responding.
No reports on effectiveness

00:30:34.895 --> 00:30:36.988
but I really can't believe
that against the Borg...

00:30:37.030 --> 00:30:38.588
Ensign Crusher,
at their current speed

00:30:38.632 --> 00:30:39.724
when will they reach Earth?

00:30:39.766 --> 00:30:41.893
27 minutes.

00:30:41.935 --> 00:30:43.732
The soonest we could intercept?

00:30:45.572 --> 00:30:47.403
42 minutes, sir.

00:30:47.441 --> 00:30:49.432
Riker to Data.

00:30:49.476 --> 00:30:50.443
What's your status?

00:30:50.477 --> 00:30:52.445
The initial
cybernetic connection

00:30:52.479 --> 00:30:56.313
into Captain Picard's neural net
pathways has been established.

00:30:56.349 --> 00:30:57.577
Mr. O'Brien is ready

00:30:57.617 --> 00:30:58.777
to process the Borg signal

00:30:58.819 --> 00:31:00.548
through the transport
pattern buffer.

00:31:00.587 --> 00:31:02.054
Make it so.

00:31:02.089 --> 00:31:03.886
With dispatch, Mr. Data.

00:31:03.924 --> 00:31:06.222
Proceeding immediately, sir.

00:31:06.259 --> 00:31:07.920
Data out.

00:31:21.875 --> 00:31:25.072
The neural link
will be established

00:31:25.112 --> 00:31:26.773
in three stages.

00:31:26.813 --> 00:31:28.212
Doctor, I suggest

00:31:28.248 --> 00:31:31.411
you closely observe
Captain Picard's life signs

00:31:31.451 --> 00:31:32.577
while, at each stage

00:31:32.619 --> 00:31:34.985
Chief O'Brien monitors
my positronic matrix activity.

00:31:35.088 --> 00:31:36.214
Counselor

00:31:36.256 --> 00:31:38.781
hopefully, you will
be able to determine

00:31:38.825 --> 00:31:40.656
whether I am reaching
Captain Picard.

00:31:40.694 --> 00:31:41.820
At what point

00:31:41.862 --> 00:31:43.625
should I shut it down
if there's a problem?

00:31:45.398 --> 00:31:46.865
I do not know.

00:31:46.900 --> 00:31:49.664
I have never done this before.

00:31:51.705 --> 00:31:54.003
Initiating first neural link.

00:31:54.074 --> 00:31:57.669
The Captain's vital signs
are stable.

00:31:59.679 --> 00:32:01.806
Positronic activity unchanged.

00:32:03.617 --> 00:32:07.053
First neural connection
is confirmed.

00:32:07.087 --> 00:32:08.554
I cannot report

00:32:08.588 --> 00:32:12.957
any significant access
to the Borg consciousness.

00:32:33.413 --> 00:32:35.278
It is confirmed.

00:32:35.315 --> 00:32:37.977
The Borg have broken through
the Mars Defense Perimeter.

00:32:38.084 --> 00:32:41.349
Enterprise now approaching
Terran system, sir.

00:32:41.388 --> 00:32:42.855
Slow to impulse.

00:32:42.889 --> 00:32:44.379
Time to intercept?

00:32:44.424 --> 00:32:46.949
23 minutes, 14 seconds, sir.

00:32:53.567 --> 00:32:58.004
Second neural connection
is confirmed.

00:32:58.071 --> 00:33:00.266
I still cannot report

00:33:00.307 --> 00:33:02.537
any significant access.

00:33:02.576 --> 00:33:05.409
Proceeding with the final link.

00:33:10.483 --> 00:33:12.917
Significant increase
in premotor area

00:33:12.953 --> 00:33:14.887
and hypothalamus activity.

00:33:14.921 --> 00:33:17.355
His heartbeat is accelerating
rapidly.

00:33:17.390 --> 00:33:19.051
Sir, your submicron
matrix activity

00:33:19.092 --> 00:33:20.457
is increasing exponentially.

00:33:20.493 --> 00:33:23.553
Neural connections complete.

00:33:23.597 --> 00:33:28.296
I have access
to the Borg subspace signals.

00:33:28.335 --> 00:33:31.202
Processing.

00:33:31.238 --> 00:33:32.728
Processing.

00:33:32.772 --> 00:33:33.761
Data.

00:33:33.807 --> 00:33:35.399
Stand by.

00:33:35.442 --> 00:33:37.376
Processing.

00:33:39.279 --> 00:33:41.213
Processing.

00:33:46.820 --> 00:33:48.447
Fascinating.

00:33:48.488 --> 00:33:52.652
The Borg group consciousness
is divided into subcommands

00:33:52.692 --> 00:33:55.593
necessary to carry out
all functions.

00:33:55.629 --> 00:34:00.225
Defense,
communication, navigation--

00:34:00.267 --> 00:34:02.235
they are all controlled

00:34:02.269 --> 00:34:05.397
by a root command
implanted into ea...

00:34:35.502 --> 00:34:37.470
Data, I'm picking up increased

00:34:37.504 --> 00:34:39.062
neural activity
in Captain Picard

00:34:39.105 --> 00:34:42.973
Iocalized in the prefrontal
and parietal lobes.

00:34:43.009 --> 00:34:43.976
The Borg might be trying

00:34:44.010 --> 00:34:45.307
to terminate
their link with him.

00:34:50.550 --> 00:34:51.847
Negative.

00:34:51.885 --> 00:34:54.945
The subspace signal
configuration is unchanged.

00:34:54.988 --> 00:34:58.754
What is causing the increased
neural activity is unclear.

00:34:58.792 --> 00:35:00.783
No, it's not.

00:35:00.827 --> 00:35:02.226
It's him.

00:35:02.262 --> 00:35:04.560
It's Picard.

00:35:11.171 --> 00:35:12.638
Troi to Bridge.

00:35:12.672 --> 00:35:15.869
Data has made first contact
with Captain Picard.

00:35:15.909 --> 00:35:17.809
Can you communicate
with him, Data?

00:35:17.844 --> 00:35:20.540
I have been unable
to create a neural path

00:35:20.580 --> 00:35:22.548
around the Borg implants, sir.

00:35:22.582 --> 00:35:24.413
It is Captain Picard himself

00:35:24.451 --> 00:35:26.953
who has somehow managed
to initiate contact.

00:35:27.086 --> 00:35:30.522
Sir, the Borg have halted
their approach to Earth.

00:35:30.556 --> 00:35:32.046
I think we got their attention.

00:35:32.091 --> 00:35:33.149
Time to intercept?

00:35:33.192 --> 00:35:35.057
Two minutes, four seconds, sir.

00:35:35.094 --> 00:35:37.187
They're worried.

00:35:37.229 --> 00:35:39.891
They're worried because
we have access to Picard.

00:35:39.932 --> 00:35:41.194
Mr. Data, we have two minutes

00:35:41.233 --> 00:35:42.860
to figure out
what we can do with it.

00:35:42.902 --> 00:35:45.735
Sir, it is clear the Borg
are either unwilling

00:35:45.771 --> 00:35:48.501
or unable to terminate
their subspace links.

00:35:48.541 --> 00:35:51.874
That may be
their Achilles heel, Captain--

00:35:51.911 --> 00:35:53.538
their interdependency.

00:35:53.579 --> 00:35:55.479
What do you mean, Doctor?

00:35:55.514 --> 00:35:57.914
He's part of their collective
consciousness now.

00:35:57.950 --> 00:36:00.077
Cutting him off would be
like asking one of us

00:36:00.119 --> 00:36:02.349
to disconnect an arm
or a foot-- we can't do it.

00:36:02.388 --> 00:36:05.186
They operate as a single mind.

00:36:05.224 --> 00:36:09.217
One of them jumps off a cliff,
they all jump off?

00:36:09.261 --> 00:36:11.286
Data, is it possible
to plant a command

00:36:11.330 --> 00:36:13.389
into the Borg
collective consciousness?

00:36:13.432 --> 00:36:14.831
It is conceivable, sir

00:36:14.867 --> 00:36:17.495
but it would require
altering the pathway

00:36:17.536 --> 00:36:19.094
from the root command

00:36:19.138 --> 00:36:21.129
to affect all iterative
branchpoints in...

00:36:21.173 --> 00:36:24.108
Make every effort, Mr. Data.

00:36:24.143 --> 00:36:26.509
Sir, what command
shall I attempt to plant?

00:36:26.545 --> 00:36:29.036
Something straightforward

00:36:29.081 --> 00:36:31.072
Iike "disarm
your weapons systems."

00:36:32.118 --> 00:36:33.551
Visual contact with the Borg.

00:36:33.586 --> 00:36:34.951
On screen.

00:36:34.987 --> 00:36:38.946
Magnify.

00:36:38.991 --> 00:36:41.323
Sensors reading increased power
generation from the Borg.

00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:42.486
Red Alert.

00:36:42.528 --> 00:36:43.961
Load all torpedo bays.

00:36:44.030 --> 00:36:44.962
Ready phasers.

00:36:45.031 --> 00:36:46.225
Aye, Captain.

00:36:46.265 --> 00:36:48.233
Status of Borg weapons.

00:36:48.267 --> 00:36:50.201
Their weapon systems
are fully charged.

00:36:50.236 --> 00:36:51.362
Data?

00:36:51.404 --> 00:36:54.532
Attempting to reroute
subcommand paths, Captain.

00:36:54.573 --> 00:36:57.872
Defense systems are protected
by access barriers.

00:37:02.782 --> 00:37:04.682
Borg attempting to lock on
tractor beam.

00:37:04.717 --> 00:37:06.514
Rotate shield frequencies.

00:37:06.552 --> 00:37:07.883
Data, report.

00:37:07.920 --> 00:37:09.046
I am unable to penetrate

00:37:09.088 --> 00:37:11.147
defense systems command
structure, Captain.

00:37:11.190 --> 00:37:12.782
Try the power systems, Data.

00:37:12.825 --> 00:37:14.918
See if you can get them
to power down.

00:37:15.027 --> 00:37:16.187
Acknowledged.

00:37:16.228 --> 00:37:19.197
Attempting new power
subcommand path.

00:37:19.231 --> 00:37:21.358
Shields have failed.

00:37:21.400 --> 00:37:23.334
They've locked on, sir.

00:37:23.369 --> 00:37:27.203
They're pulling us in.

00:37:27.239 --> 00:37:28.900
Fire all weapons.

00:37:35.714 --> 00:37:39.548
I cannot penetrate Borg
power subcommand structure, sir.

00:37:39.585 --> 00:37:41.280
All critical subcommands

00:37:41.320 --> 00:37:42.446
are protected, Captain.

00:37:42.488 --> 00:37:43.819
Then it's over.

00:37:43.856 --> 00:37:46.654
Mr. Crusher, ready a collision
course with the Borg ship.

00:37:48.360 --> 00:37:49.918
You heard me--
a collision course!

00:37:51.330 --> 00:37:52.490
Yes, sir.

00:37:52.531 --> 00:37:55.329
Mr. La Forge, prepare
to go to warp power.

00:37:55.367 --> 00:37:56.800
Aye, sir.

00:37:58.404 --> 00:37:59.996
Sleep.

00:38:02.041 --> 00:38:05.010
He's regaining consciousness.

00:38:05.044 --> 00:38:06.671
Sleep.

00:38:06.712 --> 00:38:08.407
It's Captain Picard speaking

00:38:08.447 --> 00:38:10.176
not Locutus.

00:38:10.216 --> 00:38:13.185
Sleep, Data.

00:38:13.219 --> 00:38:15.210
He's exhausted.

00:38:15.254 --> 00:38:17.347
Yes, Doctor.

00:38:17.389 --> 00:38:21.883
But if I may make a supposition,
I do not believe his message

00:38:21.927 --> 00:38:24.225
was intended to express fatigue

00:38:24.263 --> 00:38:26.788
but to suggest
a course of action.

00:38:33.639 --> 00:38:35.937
Borg cutting beam activated.

00:38:36.008 --> 00:38:38.135
Mr. Crusher.

00:38:39.812 --> 00:38:40.801
Eng...

00:38:40.846 --> 00:38:43.406
Data to Bridge.
Stand by.

00:38:43.449 --> 00:38:45.815
Stand by all stations.

00:38:45.851 --> 00:38:47.580
I am attempting to penetrate

00:38:47.620 --> 00:38:49.952
the Borg regenerative
subcommand path.

00:38:50.055 --> 00:38:54.048
It is a low-priority system
and may be accessible.

00:38:57.563 --> 00:39:00.464
Warning. Outer hull breach.

00:39:00.499 --> 00:39:02.490
Sir, shall I execute
evacuation sequence?

00:39:02.535 --> 00:39:03.502
Negative, Mr. Worf.

00:39:03.536 --> 00:39:04.901
Mr. Data, your final report.

00:39:04.970 --> 00:39:06.267
Stand by.

00:39:06.305 --> 00:39:07.499
I can't, Mr. Data!

00:39:07.540 --> 00:39:14.070
Warning. Inner hull failure
imminent on decks 23, 24 and 25.

00:39:14.113 --> 00:39:16.843
Decompression danger.

00:39:31.564 --> 00:39:34.158
Mr. Data,
what the hell happened?

00:39:34.200 --> 00:39:35.929
I successfully planted a command

00:39:36.035 --> 00:39:38.265
into the Borg
collective consciousness.

00:39:38.304 --> 00:39:39.396
It misdirected them

00:39:39.438 --> 00:39:41.599
to believe it was time
to regenerate.

00:39:41.640 --> 00:39:45.371
In effect,
I put them all to sleep.

00:39:47.913 --> 00:39:49.175
To sleep?

00:39:49.215 --> 00:39:51.877
Yes, sir.

00:39:51.917 --> 00:39:55.216
Status of Borg power drive?

00:39:57.590 --> 00:39:58.887
Minimal power.

00:39:58.924 --> 00:40:00.289
Electromagnetic field?

00:40:03.596 --> 00:40:05.063
Nonexistent.

00:40:05.097 --> 00:40:08.089
Commander Shelby,
take an away team

00:40:08.133 --> 00:40:11.591
and confirm that the Borg are...
asleep.

00:40:11.637 --> 00:40:14.105
Delighted, sir.

00:40:16.175 --> 00:40:17.767
Mr. Worf.

00:40:38.163 --> 00:40:39.755
Shelby to Enterprise.

00:40:39.798 --> 00:40:41.231
It's true.

00:40:41.266 --> 00:40:43.894
They're all
in a regeneration mode.

00:40:43.936 --> 00:40:45.403
They're dormant, sir.

00:40:45.437 --> 00:40:47.997
Any indication to how long
we can keep them like this?

00:40:48.073 --> 00:40:49.404
Checking.

00:40:51.243 --> 00:40:54.701
Tricorder readings are
fluctuating rapidly, Commander.

00:40:54.747 --> 00:40:56.715
Shelby to Enterprise.

00:40:56.749 --> 00:40:59.217
There are indications here
that their entire power net's

00:40:59.251 --> 00:41:00.513
about to feed back on itself.

00:41:00.552 --> 00:41:02.713
I'd say we're looking
at a self-destruct sequence

00:41:02.755 --> 00:41:04.347
activated
by the Borg's malfunction.

00:41:04.390 --> 00:41:06.119
Do you want us
to attempt to disarm it?

00:41:06.158 --> 00:41:09.093
Stand by.

00:41:09.128 --> 00:41:10.186
There's no way to know

00:41:10.229 --> 00:41:13.289
what the destruction of the Borg
ship will do to him.

00:41:13.332 --> 00:41:15.562
We should also
consider the advantages

00:41:15.601 --> 00:41:18.195
of further examination of the
Borg and their vessel, sir.

00:41:20.506 --> 00:41:22.133
I don't think so.

00:41:22.174 --> 00:41:24.438
Data, separate yourself
from Captain Picard.

00:41:24.476 --> 00:41:26.068
Away team, get yourselves home.

00:41:26.111 --> 00:41:28.978
Mr. Crusher, upon their return
move us to a safe position.

00:41:29.081 --> 00:41:30.673
Aye, sir.

00:41:54.440 --> 00:41:56.101
Life signs are stable.

00:41:56.141 --> 00:41:59.633
The DNA around
the microcircuit fiber implants

00:41:59.678 --> 00:42:01.475
is returning to normal.

00:42:03.148 --> 00:42:05.116
How do you feel?

00:42:08.487 --> 00:42:11.217
Almost human.

00:42:11.256 --> 00:42:15.249
With just...
a bit of a headache.

00:42:15.294 --> 00:42:16.591
We'll get you to Sick Bay.

00:42:16.628 --> 00:42:19.495
We won't have any trouble
getting those implants out now.

00:42:19.531 --> 00:42:22.398
How much do you remember?

00:42:25.604 --> 00:42:29.062
Everything.

00:42:29.108 --> 00:42:33.568
Including some brilliantly
unorthodox strategy

00:42:33.612 --> 00:42:37.139
from a former First Officer
of mine.

00:42:48.360 --> 00:42:50.157
...and Earth Station
McKinley has advised

00:42:50.195 --> 00:42:52.595
that they're ready to begin
refitting the Enterprise.

00:42:52.631 --> 00:42:53.996
And the estimated time
for repairs?

00:42:54.099 --> 00:42:55.532
Five or six weeks.

00:42:56.735 --> 00:42:58.032
-Come.
-Come.

00:43:01.206 --> 00:43:03.367
Request permission to disembark,
sir.

00:43:06.478 --> 00:43:09.038
Permission granted.

00:43:09.081 --> 00:43:12.050
They picked a fine officer
for the task force, Commander.

00:43:12.084 --> 00:43:15.247
We'll have the fleet back up
in less than a year.

00:43:15.287 --> 00:43:17.380
I imagine
you'll have your choice

00:43:17.422 --> 00:43:19.413
of any Starfleet command, sir.

00:43:21.260 --> 00:43:24.388
Everyone is so concerned
about my next job.

00:43:24.429 --> 00:43:27.193
With all due respect,
Commander... sir

00:43:27.232 --> 00:43:29.132
my career plans

00:43:29.168 --> 00:43:31.227
are my own business
and no one else's.

00:43:31.270 --> 00:43:32.897
But it's nice to know

00:43:32.938 --> 00:43:35.065
I'll have a few options.

00:43:35.107 --> 00:43:38.508
I hope I have the fortune
of serving with you again, sir.

00:43:40.846 --> 00:43:42.473
Captain.

00:43:47.352 --> 00:43:49.980
Course for Station McKinley
ready and laid in, sir.

00:43:50.088 --> 00:43:52.716
Make it so, Number One.
